/**
 * @addtogroup Foundation_BuildGuide_Linux
 *
 * Native target presets:
 *
 * @code
 * linux_gcc_x64
 * linux_clang_x64
 * linux_gcc_arm64
 * linux_clang_arm64
 * @endcode
 *
 * Foundation uses Ninja Multi-Config so Debug and Release share one build tree
 * without mixing object files or duplicating installed headers.
 * GCC and Clang are different compatibility targets and therefore use separate
 * presets and distribution directories.
 *
 * These are native presets. The x64 presets require an x86-64 Linux host and the
 * Arm64 presets require an AArch64/Arm64 Linux host. They do not install a
 * cross-compiler or sysroot and will reject a mismatched detected processor.
 *
 * Example:
 *
 * @code{bash}
 * gcc --version
 * ninja --version
 * ./scripts/configure.sh linux_gcc_x64 --fresh
 * ./scripts/build.sh linux_gcc_x64 --config Debug --target Foundation
 * ./scripts/build.sh linux_gcc_x64 --config Release --target Foundation
 * ./scripts/export.sh linux_gcc_x64 --fresh
 * @endcode
 *
 * Repeat with the Clang preset after recording `clang++ --version`. Inspect the
 * exported objects with `file`, `readelf`, or `llvm-readobj`, and compile an
 * external consumer through `Foundation::Foundation`.
 */
